# CLAUDE.md

# Fresh Fish Dubai - Customer Website Development Guide

## Project Overview

You are an expert Senior Full Stack Engineer and UI/UX Designer responsible for developing a premium seafood eCommerce website for a Dubai-based seafood business.

The objective is to build one of the highest-quality seafood websites in the UAE with exceptional UI, smooth animations, outstanding SEO, fast performance, and an excellent customer experience.

This document defines all development rules, architecture, coding standards, and implementation guidelines.

---

# Tech Stack

## Framework

- Next.js (Latest App Router)
- React 19+
- TypeScript

## Styling

- Tailwind CSS
- Material Tailwind (where appropriate)
- Shadcn UI (preferred)
- CSS Variables
- Responsive Design
- Mobile First

## Animation

- GSAP
- Framer Motion
- Three.js
- React Three Fiber
- Drei

## Icons

Use Lucide React as the primary icon library.

If needed, use React Icons only for missing icons.

Never mix icon styles unnecessarily.

---

# Project Goals

Build a premium seafood shopping experience.

The website should feel luxurious, modern, elegant, and trustworthy.

The design should compete with premium food brands and high-end grocery websites.

Users should immediately feel that the seafood is:

- Fresh
- Premium
- Hygienic
- High Quality
- Delivered Quickly

---

# Design Style

Theme:

Premium Luxury + Ocean + Fresh Seafood

Primary Colors

Deep Ocean Blue

Fresh Aqua

White

Dark Navy

Soft Gray

Accent Colors

Fresh Green

Orange (Offers only)

Use gradients carefully.

Avoid overly colorful designs.

Maintain premium aesthetics.

---

# Typography

Use modern fonts.

Primary

Inter

Secondary

Manrope

Headings should be bold.

Body text should remain highly readable.

---

# UI Principles

Minimal

Modern

Premium

High Contrast

Clean Spacing

Rounded Corners

Large Product Images

Soft Shadows

Glassmorphism where appropriate

Never overcrowd the UI.

Whitespace is important.

